--- body ---
## Context
Author 2026-10-28: "even in forge mode, human and Copilot reviews are rare, so forge mode but offline
should work without lag (lazy async)." After tracker 1298 the review writes are local, but these forge
reads still block a review, each through `gh` with a 120 s timeout (`scripts/forge.py` ~107):
- `gaze_setup.py` ~129-141: `resolve` (PR head, base, body), `comments` (discussion), `checks` (CI).
- verify-gate reads human and Copilot reviews and comments (`skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` ~53, ~294, ~505)
  and posts a pointer comment (best-effort already).
Offline or on a slow network, a review either stalls on these calls or stops.

## Design (default; the implementer may refine)
- What a review truly needs from the forge is the PR -> branch/base mapping and the head. Cache it on
  first contact (e.g. in the review's request entry on notes); later runs read the cache and refresh it in
  the background.
- Discussion, CI and human/Copilot reviews are context: fetched lazily in the background with a short
  bound; when unavailable the review proceeds and states `forge: unread (offline)` in its answer or
  verdict, never "no reviews".
- The forge read that can change a verdict (unresolved human review comments) is rechecked at landing,
  which needs the forge anyway: `raid_land` refuses (or routes to the gate) when a human or Copilot review
  newer than the gate's read is unresolved.
- No new setting: behaviour follows reachability.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] With the forge unreachable, gaze and verify-gate on a PR whose mapping is cached complete without waiting on a forge timeout; the answer/verdict says the forge context was unread; tests (stub forge that hangs or fails).
- [ ] A first-ever review of a PR with the forge unreachable stops with a clear message (it cannot map the PR), consistent with ticket 1300's fail-closed first discovery.
- [ ] Landing rechecks human and Copilot reviews newer than the gate's read and refuses on an unresolved one; test.
- [ ] Skill texts (gaze, verify-gate, merge) describe the lazy reads; `make check` passes.
